    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0221" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg161"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-16"><hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2402.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a telegram received to-day from Consul Hixson, giving a summary of the number
                    of participants in the Kutien massacre who have been arrested and convicted and
                    who are still at large. From this it appears that 43 convictions have been
                    secured, 7 executions have taken place, 139 are under arrest, and 100 and more
                    participants in the outrage are still at large.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d175-a1.xml" xpointer="d175-a1"/>
            </div>
